CloudBurrow patch 98 to github.com/goccy/bigquery-emulator v0.8.1
(cloudburrow/cloudburrow#1814). Applies after patch 0096; needs
googlesqlite patch 0097.

A query parameter in the select list has its declared type in BigQuery
(https://cloud.google.com/bigquery/docs/parameterized-queries). The REST
API gives every scalar parameter as text; INT64, FLOAT64, BOOL and
TIMESTAMP were bound as Go values of their type, the others as strings, so
`SELECT @p` of a BYTES, NUMERIC, BIGNUMERIC, DATE, TIME, GEOGRAPHY, JSON or
INTERVAL was a STRING and of a DATETIME a TIMESTAMP. They are bound as
googlesqlite.TypedParameter (googlesqlite patch 0097), a value of their own
type.

server/cloudburrow_typed_parameters_test.go (TestTypedScalarParameters:
every scalar type, positional and named, alone in the select list).

